WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.988
Here's how the normalizer maps them.

2
00:00:01.988 --> 00:00:04.526
A post tagged Retirement is a retirement.

3
00:00:04.526 --> 00:00:07.813
Plan-for-change and
prevent-or-fix posts are changes,

4
00:00:07.813 --> 00:00:10.337
and stay-informed posts are advisories.

5
00:00:10.337 --> 00:00:13.933
For all of them, if Microsoft
set an action-required date,

6
00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:17.138
the record keeps it, and
says the provider decided.

7
00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:22.494
There's one kit rule: a prevent-or-fix post
with no date is still action required,

8
00:00:22.494 --> 00:00:25.674
labeled as the kit's rule,
with no date invented.

9
00:00:25.674 --> 00:00:29.329
Service health issues become
incidents or advisories,

10
00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.880
never action required, and
a resolved issue is closed.
